      "solution": "n,k=list(map(int,input().split()))\nu=[0]+list(map(int,input().split()))\nwhile k>n:\n    q,r=divmod(k,n+1)\n    if r==0:\n        k=q\n    else:\n        k-=q\nprint(u[k])",
      "statement": "You have to find the [[k]]-th value of a sequence whose {{n}} first terms are given.\nThe next terms are defined by these {{n}} first terms in a weird way.\nIf you decimate each term every {{n+1}} values, the sequence built on the remaining terms is the same than the original sequence.\nMore surprising: the decimated terms also yields the original sequence.",
