    "statementHTML": "<div class=\"statement-body\">\n<div class=\"statement-section statement-goal\">\n   <h2><span class=\"icon icon-goal\">&nbsp;</span><span>Goal </span></h2>\n   <span class=\"question-statement\">You have to find the <var>k</var>-th value of a sequence whose <const>n</const> first terms are given.<br>The next terms are defined by these <const>n</const> first terms in a weird way.<br>If you decimate each term every <const>n+1</const> values, the sequence built on the remaining terms is the same than the original sequence.<br>More surprising: the decimated terms also yields the original sequence.</span>\n</div>\n<div class=\"statement-section statement-protocol\">\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Input</div>\n      <div class=\"question-statement-input\"><strong>Line 1 :</strong> <const>n</const> and <var>k</var><br><strong>Line 2:</strong> The <var>n</var> first terms of the sequence</div>\n   </div>\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Output</div>\n      <div class=\"question-statement-output\">The <var>k</var>-th term of the sequence (beware, the first term&rsquo;s rank of the sequence is 1)</div>\n   </div>\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Constraints</div>\n      <div class=\"question-statement-constraints\">0&lt;n&lt;10<br>0&lt;k&lt;10&sup1;⁰</div>\n   </div>\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Example</div>\n      <div class=\"statement-inout\">\n         <div class=\"statement-inout-in\">\n            <div class=\"title\">Input</div>\n            <pre class=\"question-statement-example-in\">4 1\n1 2 3 4</pre>\n         </div>\n         <div class=\"statement-inout-out\">\n            <div class=\"title\">Output</div>\n            <pre class=\"question-statement-example-out\">1</pre>\n         </div>\n      </div>\n   </div>\n</div>"
